  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Kritisch-Watten. Logic: Trick-taking with permanent trumps. Key: Three Criticals always win. Partners signal holdings. No follow-suit required except on Haube lead.',
    Player: 'Kritisch-Watten is a popular Alpine trick-taking game played in partnerships. The three Critical cards (King of Hearts, Seven of Bells, Seven of Acorns) are permanent trumps above all others. Partners use secret signals (Deuten) to communicate which Criticals they hold. Win 3 of 5 tricks to score points. Game is played to 11 points.',
    objective: 'Each partnership aims to win at least three of the five tricks in each hand; the team that does so scores points (typically two unless the stake was raised), and the first team to reach 11 points wins the game.',
    gameplay: "1. Usually, there is NO obligation to follow suit or rank.\n2. **Exception (Trump Lead)**: If the 'Haube' (the principal trump) is led, others MUST play a trump if they have one.",
    keyRules: [
      'The three Criticals (Kritische Karten) are permanent trumps: King of Hearts (Maxl), Seven of Bells (Belli), Seven of Acorns (Spitz)',
      'Forehand chooses the Schlag (rank), dealer chooses the Farbe (suit)',
      'No obligation to follow suit except when the Haube is led',
      "Players can 'offer' to raise the stake during play",
    ],
